# swing-anim.xrs - the sword hand-back by attack source (VR-220): does a TRIGGER attack
# play the game's swing on the tracked hand, and does a PHYSICAL swing keep the hand on
# the controller? And does a trigger attack's hand-back leave the swing gate open?
#
# Needs the same as swing-edge.xrs: a loaded level in GAMEPLAY (not a menu, not the
# title's attract scene - look at an xrsim-shot first), [Mode] GamepadOnly=0, and a build
# with the `anim melee` words. Run:  .\tools\xrsim-run.ps1 -Path .\tools\xrsim\swing-anim.xrs
#
# How to read a failure: `anim/melee: attack source=TRIGGER|SWING` is the verdict, one line
# per attack (or per combo clip), with the fire-to-entry time and the pulse state that
# decided it. A TRIGGER attack must say `hand-back ON`; a SWING must say `hand-back off`
# unless HandAnimMeleeSwing=1. `features.anim.meleeSource` is the same verdict in
# status.json. A `swing: BLOCKED ... owns the body` right after a trigger attack is the
# gate fault this change removes (the gate now reads the body-owning classifier only).
#
# The hand is only ever MOVED here, never placed: `hand r grip pose` teleports it, and a
# teleport is a tracking jump, which the swing detector discards on purpose.

# The sword has to be in the hand. With it sheathed the first pull draws it; with it drawn
# this is one ordinary attack. Either way the sword is out afterwards.
hand r to grip 0.25 1.30 -0.40 0 0 0 1200
@wait 1500
trigger r pull 300
@wait 2500
@mod swing on; swing mode edge; swing threshold 3.6; swing rearm 1.0; swing cooldown 300; swing rel on; swing filter median; swing sword on; swing output rt
@wait 800
@mod anim handback on; anim melee on; anim melee swing off
@wait 1000
@mark

# 1. A trigger attack: the source is TRIGGER and the hand goes to the game's clip.
trigger r pull 300
@log anim/melee: attack source=TRIGGER -> hand-back ON
@modassert features.anim.meleeSource eq trigger
@modassert features.anim.handAnimMelee eq true
@wait 1800
@nolog swing: FIRE
@mark

# 2. A physical swing: the same 0.68 m in 200 ms peaks near 5 m/s. The source is SWING,
#    the hand stays on the controller, and the game still honours the attack.
hand r to grip -0.35 1.00 -0.45 0 0 0 900
@wait 1500
@mark
hand r to grip 0.25 1.30 -0.40 0 0 0 200
@log swing: FIRE #\d+ slash
@log anim/melee: attack source=SWING \(swing #\d+\) -> hand-back off
@log swing: HONOURED slash
@modassert features.anim.meleeSource eq swing
@wait 1800
@mark

# 3. A physical swing right after a trigger attack is NOT refused by the body gate: the
#    trigger attack's hand-back is a hand pose, not the game owning the body.
trigger r pull 300
@log anim/melee: attack source=TRIGGER -> hand-back ON
@wait 120
hand r to grip -0.35 1.00 -0.45 0 0 0 200
@wait 1200
@nolog swing: BLOCKED .*owns the body
@wait 1500
@mark

# 4. The lever for the other rule: with HandAnimMeleeSwing=1 a swing hands back too.
#    The seam write lands up to a second after the line (1 Hz poll), and a Debug build
#    can starve the hand of samples for a moment right after it: rest, then swing.
@mod anim melee swing on
@wait 2000
hand r to grip -0.35 1.00 -0.45 0 0 0 600
@wait 1500
@mark
hand r to grip 0.25 1.30 -0.40 0 0 0 200
@log swing: FIRE #\d+ slash
@log anim/melee: attack source=SWING \(swing #\d+\) -> hand-back ON \(HandAnimMeleeSwing=1\)
@wait 1800
@mod anim melee swing off
@wait 1200
@mark

# 5. The master off: a trigger attack names its source and says why the hand stays.
@mod anim melee off
@wait 600
@mark
trigger r pull 300
@log anim/melee: attack source=TRIGGER .*HandAnimMelee=0, the hand stays on the controller
@modassert features.anim.handAnimMelee eq false
@wait 1500
@mod anim melee on
@wait 300
@mod anim melee status
